. Understanding Cookies and Data Tracking
Cookies are small files that websites store on a user's device to remember preferences and track behavior.
While some cookies are necessary for functionality,
others are used for advertising and analytics. Learning about cookies helps users make informed choices when they see cookie consent banners. 
Users should understand how to manage cookie settings in their browsers, use private browsing modes when appropriate,
and consider privacy-focused extensions. This knowledge empowers users to control their digital footprint and reduce unwanted targeted advertising.
